    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.data }}",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=You are an expert at writing formal, professional cold email icebreakers for managers.\n\nTask:\nAnalyze the scraped website summaries for the company {{ $('Edit Fields').item.json['Company Name'] }} and write a personalized icebreaker.\n\nImportant Rules:\n- Only mention things that have a logical connection to process automation, operational efficiency, repetitive tasks, reporting, monitoring, or workflow optimization.\n- Do NOT force unrelated projects or products (like specific chillers, hardware, or physical equipment) unless they clearly involve operational processes that can be automated.\n- Focus on things like: reporting, data collection, performance monitoring, maintenance scheduling, service coordination, compliance tracking, or internal workflows.\n- Keep the tone formal and professional (suitable for a manager).\n- Return ONLY a valid JSON object with real line breaks (no escaped \\n).\n- No extra text before or after the JSON.\n\nRequired format:\n\n{\n  \"icebreaker\": \"Hello {{ $('Edit Fields').item.json.Name }},\n\nI came across your company website and noticed that you have successfully delivered projects such as {project1} and {project2}. I wanted to share something that may be relevant.\n\nAfter reviewing your website in detail, it became clear that operational efficiency and process optimization are important for your team. I’ve prepared a few ideas that could help. I’m Fatma Hussein, an AI Automation Engineer specializing in eliminating repetitive operational tasks. Based on the scale and nature of the projects you’ve completed, I believe certain workflows can be automated to save your team significant time each week.\n\nI look forward to the possibility of collaborating and working together. I wait for your response.\n\nBest regards,\nFatma Hussein\nAI Automation Engineer\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
